From: horms+renesas@verge.net.au (Simon Horman)
Date: Mon,  4 Apr 2016 10:23:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 29/47] ARM: dts: r8a7793: Reference both DMA controllers in
 QSPI node
In-Reply-To: <cover.1459732726.git.horms+renesas@verge.net.au>
References: <cover.1459732726.git.horms+renesas@verge.net.au>
Message-ID: <84eba917433c9b4224adb013f36b5aa5cf5bf093.1459732726.git.horms+renesas@verge.net.au>
To: linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
List-Id: linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org

From: Niklas S?derlund <niklas.soderlund+renesas@ragnatech.se>

R-Car Gen2 have two DMA controllers, which are equivalent. Add
references to both dmac0 and dmac1 so the driver can fallback to the
later if the first one is unavailable.

Signed-off-by: Niklas S?derlund <niklas.soderlund+renesas@ragnatech.se>
Acked-by: Geert Uytterhoeven <geert+renesas@glider.be>
Signed-off-by: Simon Horman <horms+renesas@verge.net.au>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7793.dtsi | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7793.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7793.dtsi
index 88164ac44929..b16b0cca638c 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7793.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7793.dtsi
@@ -785,8 +785,9 @@
 		reg = <0 0xe6b10000 0 0x2c>;
 		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 184 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 		clocks = <&mstp9_clks R8A7793_CLK_QSPI_MOD>;
-		dmas = <&dmac0 0x17>, <&dmac0 0x18>;
-		dma-names = "tx", "rx";
+		dmas = <&dmac0 0x17>, <&dmac0 0x18>,
+		       <&dmac1 0x17>, <&dmac1 0x18>;
+		dma-names = "tx", "rx", "tx", "rx";
 		power-domains = <&cpg_clocks>;
 		num-cs = <1>;
 		#address-cells = <1>;
-- 
2.1.4
